00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  unbelievably the 2020 release of Dragon  Ball Z Kakarot means that we've now had  console games based on the massively  successful manga and anime series for  the last five decades the most recent  time 2018 s Dragon Ball fighters also  happens to be the best of a very large  bunch setting a new benchmark for  recreating the show's spectacularly  kinetic battles albeit within the  confines of a three-on-three fighter  [Music]  Kakarot has no such confines this is  Dragon Ball Z on an unprecedented scale  covering the full nine season anime saga  in such detail that describing it as  comprehensive would be doing it a  disservice  it's an action RPG that retails all of  the major arcs of the series as many DBZ  games have done before but it also  explores never before told backstories  and non-canon scenarios all approved by  crater akira toriyama you're about to  learn the hard way that effort alone  isn't enough to reach my level for the  uninitiated Kakarot is to Goku as kal-el  is to Superman and while that suggests  an adventure devoted solely to the  happy-go-lucky inhumanly powerful Sion  you'll actually get to spend time  controlling other regulars including his  son gohan and arch-nemesis turned  comrades Vegeta and piccolo Dragon Balls  vision of a futuristic earth or dragon  world as it's become known is available  to explore in its entirety and you'll be  grateful that everyone can fly once you  see just how fast it is situated between  DB Z's trademark open plains and rocky  valleys are key areas like West city  calm a house and the sights of the  legendary World Martial Arts Tournament  these are fully explorable and teeming  with NPCs as our incidental locations  such as ginger town whose population was  once fully absorbed by imperfect cell  the series off world locations aren't  ignored either in keeping with Kakarot  s-- beyond faithful adherence to the  source material you'll also travel to  Namak King Kai's tiny planet and even  Dragon Balls decidedly bureaucratic  version of the afterlife of the world of  course one of the main things you'll do  throughout these worlds is engage in ki  blast hurling afterimage dashing meaty  or combination inflicting battles but  we'll save the specifics for a future  video so what else can you get up to  when you're not decimating mountains  with a misplaced spirit bomb  quite  it turns out one of your main jobs  outside of combat is playing at  hunter-gatherer you can hunt wildlife  get the fruits and vegetables and even  try your hand at fishing this being a  dragon ball game though everything's a  little unconventional hunting is less  stealthily taking down a buck with a  rifle and more loudly battering a t-rex  with a Kamehameha while fishing is a  case of Goku using his prehensile monkey  tail which he can now reattach to his  buck for some reason and dangling it in  water until you catch a gigantic flying  catfish and fling it skyward oh and then  you execute a flying kick on the fish to  smash it into the jetty  because Dragon Ball occasionally certain  areas of the world will enter a frenzied  state which means that foraged goods  will be more abundant for a limited time  yes even the humble apple can enter a  frenzied state such is the exaggerated  nature of dragon world the real reason  for performing these activities is tied  to cooking by stopping it campfires  dotted all over the map characters can  rustle up meals that provide useful  temporary stat boosts that can make all  the difference in battle  true to its action RPG status Kakarot is  also rife with side quests and minigames  to keep you distracted from the main  storyline so what if freeze is about to  annihilate Planet Namek when there's  baseball to be played for those who feel  like they've watched and played through  the Dragon Ball Z sagas countless times  already  Kakarot side quests are a major addition  providing new glimpses into the universe  by way of giving minor characters  increased screen time and fleshing out  previously implied or never before  mentioned backstories and events the  game even plays long-overdue homage the  DB Z's filler episodes including fan  favorite Goku's ordeal where our sign  hero and piccolo both attempt to earn  their driving license with predictably  destructive consequences and finally of  course there are the seven titular  Dragon Balls to discover - just like the  series they are scattered far and wide  across the land and by successfully  gathering them all together you'll be  granted one wish by the mighty dragon  Shenron keep an eye out for future  Dragon Ball Z Kakarot videos where we'll  be taking a deep dive into its combat  and looking at the growth and evolution  of its playable characters over the  course of its huge campaign

